                                        </box>
                                        <box autoresizesSubviews="NO" borderType="line" title="Lenz Address Correction:" id="861">
                                            <rect key="frame" x="309" y="258" width="500" height="136"/>
                                            <autoresizingMask key="autoresizingMask" flexibleMaxX="YES" flexibleMinY="YES"/>
                                            <view key="contentView" id="vU1-XD-UuY">
                                                <rect key="frame" x="0.0" y="0.0" width="500" height="124"/>
                                                <autoresizingMask key="autoresizingMask" widthSizable="YES" heightSizable="YES"/>
                                                <subviews>
                                                    <textField focusRingType="none" verticalHuggingPriority="750" horizontalCompressionResistancePriority="250" id="865">
                                                        <rect key="frame" x="15" y="39" width="476" height="80"/>
                                                        <autoresizingMask key="autoresizingMask" flexibleMaxX="YES" flexibleMinY="YES"/>
                                                        <textFieldCell key="cell" controlSize="mini" sendsActionOnEndEditing="YES" id="866">
                                                            <font key="font" metaFont="system"/>
                                                            <string key="title">It seems that different manufacturers use different conventions to code the address bits within DCC packets. Command Systems like the Roco 10764 starts with 0, whereas the Lenz LZV100 start with 1. In addition, the Lenz LZV100 seems to behave incorrect if the address is exactly 0, 64, 128 or 192. To compensate for this, a special Command System CV was added.</string>
                                                            <color key="textColor" name="controlTextColor" catalog="System" colorSpace="catalog"/>
                                                            <color key="backgroundColor" name="controlColor" catalog="System" colorSpace="catalog"/>
                                                        </textFieldCell>
                                                    </textField>
                                                </subviews>
                                            </view>
                                        </box>
                                        <box autoresizesSubviews="NO" borderType="line" title="Decoder Mode:" id="862">
                                            <rect key="frame" x="309" y="50" width="500" height="176"/>
                                            <autoresizingMask key="autoresizingMask" flexibleMaxX="YES" flexibleMinY="YES"/>
                                            <view key="contentView" id="J9s-Zm-5vk">
                                                <rect key="frame" x="0.0" y="0.0" width="500" height="164"/>
                                                <autoresizingMask key="autoresizingMask" widthSizable="YES" heightSizable="YES"/>
                                                <subviews>
                                                    <textField focusRingType="none" verticalHuggingPriority="750" horizontalCompressionResistancePriority="250" id="867">
                                                        <rect key="frame" x="11" y="10" width="476" height="144"/>
                                                        <autoresizingMask key="autoresizingMask" flexibleMaxX="YES" flexibleMinY="YES"/>
                                                        <textFieldCell key="cell" controlSize="mini" sendsActionOnEndEditing="YES" id="868">
                                                            <font key="font" metaFont="system"/>
                                                            <string key="title">The decoder can be used in the following modes:
- Swith decoder
- Swith decoder plus (has an Emergency board)
- Servo decoder
- Relais decoder for 4 relais
- Relais decoder for 16 relais
- Safety decoder with Watchdog
- Liftdecoder
- Function</string>
                                                            <color key="textColor" name="controlTextColor" catalog="System" colorSpace="catalog"/>
                                                            <color key="backgroundColor" name="controlColor" catalog="System" colorSpace="catalog"/>
                                                        </textFieldCell>
                                                    </textField>
                                                </subviews>
                                            </view>
                                        </box>
